// Comment: The test is about Remove method. In the method, 'x' is removed from the list 'arrList'. Preconditions to test are that 'x' is in the list before removal, 'arrList' is not empty after operation, and 'arrList' does not contain 'x' after removal.
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == true && New_arrListContainsX == false && New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount - 1);
// Comment: The test is about Insert method. In the method, 'x' is inserted at the index 'index' in the list 'arrList'. Preconditions to test are that 'x' is not in the list before insertion, index is a valid position, 'arrList' contains 'x' at index after insertion, and the length of 'arrList' is increased by one.
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == false && Old_index >= 0 && Old_index <= New_arrListCount && New_arrListContainsX == true && New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1);
// Comment: The test is about Set method. In the method, 'x' is set at the index 'index' in the list 'arrList'. Preconditions to test are that 'x' is not in the index 'index' before operation, 'arrList' contains 'x' at index after operation, and index is a valid position.
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == false && New_arrListContainsX == true && Old_index >= 0 && Old_index < New_arrListCount);
// Comment: The last assertion is about the Set method. After testing, we found that the last index of 'x' in the new array is not same as the old array size. There might be a bug in our assert statement.
